      "message": "I\u0027m late to the party, but one of the things I\u0027ve liked about using merge commits is that it doesn\u0027t generate emails for the people who were working on the original CLs, like cherry picks does. Collecting all the bugs for the merged CLs and putting them in the merge commit message generates Buganizer comments, which turn into emails for everyone CCed on the bug. It\u0027s maybe half the amount of email generated by cherry-picking, but it can still be substantial.\n\nThoughts on the benefits vs the costs of adding this to the commit message?",
